# Line endings.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the default on a Windows install, and it rewrites
# every checked-out text file to CRLF. For most of this repository that is
# harmless. For `.mjs` it is not: Vitest loads those files as real ES modules
# rather than transforming them, and a CRLF module fails to parse with
#
#     SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token
#
# pointing at the *import* line in the test that pulls it in — which reads like
# a broken test file and not like a line ending. `whatsapp-business-profile`
# failed that way on every Windows checkout while passing in CI, for long
# enough that it was written off as "expected here".
#
# Checking these out with LF everywhere costs nothing and removes a whole class
# of failure that only ever appears on one operating system.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf

# The same rule, for the files that are copied to the server and run there.
#
# `site-block.awk` is executed by awk on the VPS and its output is written back
# as the nginx configuration of the live site; the `.conf` files under
# `services/media-processor/nginx/` are read by nginx itself. Neither is loaded
# by this repository's tooling, so a CRLF checkout would travel all the way to
# production before anything noticed — and the fixtures beside them are compared
# byte-for-byte by `nginx-site-block.test.ts`, which is where it would show up
# as a test that passes on Linux and fails on Windows.
*.awk  text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
